sg-session (0.1.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remote Desktop (E1, ADR 0010): sg-rdp-authd streams the user's session.
    After PAM accepts a user, its root monitor finds or starts that user's
    remote session (headless sg-compositor at the client's size, a seat and
    lock service of its own) and passes the RDP side a connection to the
    compositor's privileged socket. Frames by screencopy as uncompressed
    bitmap updates; keyboard and pointer by virtual devices. Disconnect keeps
    the session; the next login reconnects. sg-rdpd.service, installed
    disabled; certificate made on first start. Gate: make test-rdp-stream.
  * sg-brokerd finds a requester's Remote Desktop seat as well as the console.
  * Domain controller role (D2): sg-dc-provision makes the machine a Samba AD
    DC with internal DNS (realm, NetBIOS domain, host name, Administrator
    password on stdin), points its resolver at itself, and waits until its
    identity mapping answers. Gate: sg-image make dc-test.
  * Domain member (D1): sg-domain-join joins an AD domain (winbind, Kerberos
    ticket at sign-in for Wine's SSPI, sg-domain-groups making Domain Users
    the Windows system's users and Domain Admins its administrators at each
    sign-in). sg-sspi-probe.exe for the gate (sg-image make domain-test).

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:12:03 -0700

sg-session (0.1.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-install: installs Stained Glass from the live system (the stick's
    "live" entry) onto a disk -- systemd-repart block copy, the root grown to
    the disk, a fresh machine identity, the owner as administrator, no lab
    account, no live entry. Depends on systemd-repart and e2fsprogs.
  * Setup: on a live boot the login screen is replaced by the installation
    wizard (sg-setup.exe), which asks sg-installd -- a root service behind a
    socket only the login screen's account can reach -- to run sg-install.
    Gate: make test-setup; sg-image's make install-test drives it in a VM.

 -- Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:40:55 -0700

